title: The pitch page twice promises something "below" that is not on it, and the gentlest pages are reached only through 'README-old.org', which nothing links.
pid: 700be5f2-07a5-4fd1-989d-d984cebe126f
body: |2-
  'this-is-awesome.org' says how skg allows reshaping another's data
  "is described below", and "See 'the data model' below"; neither is
  on the page, which seems cut from a longer one. 'vocabulary.org'
  (trees, nodes and links, from what a reader already has (b)),
  'hyperlinks.org' (a small tree about eggs (d)), 'FAQ.org' and every
  essay but the pitch are linked only from 'README-old.org'. So the
  pages most like Jeff's way of explaining are the ones a stranger
  following links never sees.
  Change: point both "below"s at 'data-model_friendly.org', and link
  'vocabulary.org' and 'FAQ.org' from 'docs/README.org'.
